<title>UK: Kvaerner sells UK retail centre.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner sells UK retail centre.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian shipbuilding and engineering group Kvaerner ASA said on Monday its Trafalgar House Property Ltd unit exchanged contracts to sell its only major retail investment for 18.85 million stg to Grosvenor Asset Management.  </p>
<p>The 85,000 square-foot shopping centre at Romford in southeast England had annual rental income of about 1.7 million stg, the company said.</p>
<p>The price represented an initial yield of about nine percent, Kvaerner said in a statement released here.</p>
<p>The company previously stated its medium-term plan to divest Trafalgar House's non-core property interests.</p>
